\"How This Calculator Works\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"space-y-4\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"0\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"North Carolina charges a flat 4.5% income tax rate for 2026. One rate, no brackets, no surprises. The state has been steadily reducing its flat rate over the past few years, dropping from 5.25% down to the current 4.5%. North Carolina offers a standard deduction of $12,750 for single filers and $25,500 for married filing jointly — that's one of the highest state standard deductions in the country, which softens the impact of the flat rate considerably.\\\"}}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"1\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"Let's run the numbers. A single person earning $75,000: after the $12,750 standard deduction, taxable income is $62,250. North Carolina tax comes to $2,801.25. Add federal tax and FICA, and you're looking at roughly $58,500 take-home. That's competitive with most flat-tax states, and the generous standard deduction means lower-income earners pay very little state tax.\\\"}}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"2\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"North Carolina doesn't tax Social Security benefits at the state level, which is good news for retirees. Property taxes average about 0.82% — quite reasonable. The combined state and local sales tax averages around 7.1%. Compared to \\u003ca href=\\\\\\\"/georgia-tax-calculator\\\\\\\"\\u003eGeorgia's 5.49%\\u003c/a\\u003e or \\u003ca href=\\\\\\\"/illinois-tax-calculator\\\\\\\"\\u003eIllinois' 4.95%\\u003c/a\\u003e, North Carolina's 4.5% rate is actually the lowest among neighboring flat-tax states. \\u003ca href=\\\\\\\"/relocation-calculator\\\\\\\"\\u003eRun the relocation calculator\\u003c/a\\u003e to compare for your specific salary.\\\"}}]]}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-emerald-500/5 p-6 sm:p-8\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"How It's Calculated\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"space-y-5\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h3\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 mb-2\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Formula\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"rounded-lg bg-background/50 border border-border/30 p-4 font-mono text-sm text-foreground\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"NC State Tax = (Gross Income − NC Standard Deduction) × 4.5%\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h3\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 mb-2\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Step-by-Step\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"ol\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"space-y-2\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",\\\"0\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"flex gap-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/20 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\\\",\\\"children\\\":1}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Subtract NC standard deduction ($12,750 single / $25,500 married) from gross income\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",\\\"1\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"flex gap-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-500/20 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400\\\",\\\"children\\\":2}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"span\\\",n