uted-foreground max-w-2xl mx-auto\",\"children\":\"Calculate your 2026 North Carolina take-home pay after 4.5% flat state tax, federal tax & FICA. Standard deduction $12,750. No sign-up.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"Last reviewed: January 2026 · Tax data verified against IRS Publication 15-T & state revenue departments\"}]]}]\n22:[\"$\",\"$L27\",null,{\"componentKey\":\"northcarolina\"}]\n23:[\"$\",\"$L28\",null,{\"calculatorType\":\"northcarolina\",\"calculatorSlug\":\"north-carolina-tax-calculator\"}]\n24:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-8 rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-emerald-500/5 p-6 sm:p-8\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-lg font-semibold text-foreground mb-3\",\"children\":\"Related Tools & Resources\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L10\",\"/paycheck-calculator\",{\"href\":\"/paycheck-calculator\",\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2 rounded-lg p-2 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"💵\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Paycheck Calculator\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"Full take-home pay breakdown\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L10\",\"/georgia-tax-calculator\",{\"href\":\"/georgia-tax-calculator\",\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2 rounded-lg p-2 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"🏠\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Georgia Calculator\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"Compare GA 5.49% vs NC 4.5%\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L10\",\"/relocation-calculator\",{\"href\":\"/relocation-calculator\",\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2 rounded-lg p-2 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"📊\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Relocation Calculator\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"Compare NC to other states\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L10\",\"/salary\",{\"href\":\"/salary\",\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2 rounded-lg p-2 hover:bg-emerald-500/10 transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"💰\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Salary After Tax\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"Take-home pay at every level\"}]]}]]}]]}]]}]\n25:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 space-y-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-6 sm:p-8\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"How This Calculator Works\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"North Carolina charges a flat 4.5% income tax rate for 2026. One rate, no brackets, no surprises. The state has been steadily reducing its flat rate over the past few years, dropping from 5.25% down to the current 4.5%. North Carolina offers a standard deduction of $12,750 for single filers and $25,500 for married filing jointly — that's one of the highest state standard deductions in the country, which softens the impact of the flat rate considerably.\"}}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Let's run the numbers. A single person earning $75,000: after the $12,750 standard deduction, taxable income is $62,250. North Carolina tax comes to $2,801.25. Add federal tax and FICA, and you're looking at roughly $58,500 take-home. That's competitive with most flat-tax states, and the generous standard deduction means lower-income earners pay very little state tax.\"}}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"North Carolina doesn't tax Social Security benefits at the state level, which is good news for retirees. Property taxes average about 0.82% — quite reasonable. The combined state and local sales tax averages around 7.1%. Compared to <a href=\\\"/georgia-tax-calculator\\\">Georgia's 5.49%</a> or <a href=\\\"/illinois-tax-calculator\\\">Illinois' 4.95%</a>, North Carolina's 4.5% rate is actually the lowest among neighboring flat-tax states. <a href=\\\"/relocation-calculator\\\">Run the relocation calculator</a> to compare for your specific salary.\"}}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-emerald-500/5 p-6 sm:p-8\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"How It's Calculated\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 mb-2\",\"children\":\"Formula\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg bg-background/50 border border-border/30 p-4 font-mono text-sm text-foreground\",\"children\":\"NC State Tax = (Gross Income − NC Standard Deduction) × 4.5%\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 mb-2\",\"children\":\"Step-by-Step\"}],[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"0\",{\"className\